WEBVTT

00:00:01.480 --> 00:00:02.850
Yachts.

00:00:02.850 --> 00:00:05.230
In the past, they sailed the seven seas,

00:00:05.230 --> 00:00:09.300
but in this era, they fly through outer space

00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:12.530
with the help of solar winds or interstellar medium.

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:16.120
And the people who pilot them are also flying,

00:00:16.120 --> 00:00:19.870
hoping to meet any possibility they can.

00:00:20.690 --> 00:00:21.870
Dinghies!

00:00:22.970 --> 00:00:26.090
They're a little old, but they're nice ships.

00:00:26.090 --> 00:00:29.170
President, can I take them out?

00:00:29.170 --> 00:00:30.510
Out to do what?

00:00:30.510 --> 00:00:32.010
I want to pilot them.

00:02:10.690 --> 00:02:12.070
I want to do it!

00:02:14.150 --> 00:02:15.440
What's going on?

00:02:15.440 --> 00:02:16.780
I could hear you from the hallway.

00:02:17.070 --> 00:02:18.530
Sorry!

00:02:19.490 --> 00:02:20.530
What's going on?

00:02:20.530 --> 00:02:21.620
Look at this.

00:02:22.450 --> 00:02:22.910
Come, celestial maidens! Glory shines for you!
Swoop down, ride the wind, and claim victory!

00:02:22.910 --> 00:02:26.000
The 19th Nebula Cup?

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:29.170
Sounds good! Let's do it.

00:02:29.170 --> 00:02:31.500
We have those dinghies too.

00:02:31.500 --> 00:02:33.040
It looks fun.

00:02:33.040 --> 00:02:34.550
Doesn't it? Doesn't it?

00:02:34.550 --> 00:02:35.340
Right?

00:02:35.340 --> 00:02:38.090
I've been really wanting to do this for a while.

00:02:38.090 --> 00:02:38.840
Really?

00:02:38.840 --> 00:02:39.680
What's going on?

00:02:40.090 --> 00:02:41.470
Let us in on it!

00:02:42.390 --> 00:02:44.600
But when does it start?

00:02:44.600 --> 00:02:47.520
In two weeks. Why?

00:02:47.520 --> 00:02:51.310
It might overlap with my work on the Bentenmaru.

00:02:51.310 --> 00:02:54.270
Oh, yeah. You have your job.

00:02:55.570 --> 00:02:58.190
Entering's fine, but...

00:02:58.190 --> 00:03:00.820
Is there a problem?

00:03:00.820 --> 00:03:04.240
Anyone who's actually piloted a dinghy before, raise your hand.

00:03:04.240 --> 00:03:05.370
I have!

00:03:10.750 --> 00:03:13.460
I've spent lots of time in a simulator.

00:03:15.920 --> 00:03:19.010
And you think you're ready for a tournament?

00:03:19.010 --> 00:03:20.130
What a joke!

00:03:22.590 --> 00:03:23.640
Kane?

00:03:23.640 --> 00:03:25.300
Why are you dressed like that?

00:03:26.850 --> 00:03:29.310
No time and no actual experience.

00:03:29.310 --> 00:03:31.480
You have nothing.

00:03:32.310 --> 00:03:33.810
If I don't help you...

00:03:34.590 --> 00:03:35.650
No one else will!

00:03:35.650 --> 00:03:37.650
Listen to me!

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:39.030
Help with what?

00:03:39.030 --> 00:03:41.240
You need an advisor, right?

00:03:42.070 --> 00:03:45.280
Y-Yeah. It's true, we don't have one.

00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:48.370
Then I'll do it.

00:03:48.370 --> 00:03:49.700
Kane, you can't do this without asking.

00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:53.880
A teaching credential?

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:57.130
I renewed my teaching credentials.

00:03:57.130 --> 00:04:00.210
From this moment on, I am your PE teacher!

00:04:00.470 --> 00:04:02.220
PE teacher?

00:04:06.970 --> 00:04:08.600
No more!

00:04:08.600 --> 00:04:11.270
Save me!

00:04:11.560 --> 00:04:14.480
Kane, isn't this setting a bit high?

00:04:14.480 --> 00:04:17.520
This is a recreation of the strongest typhoon ever recorded,

00:04:17.520 --> 00:04:19.690
Francisco II!

00:04:19.690 --> 00:04:24.240
No! I'm asking what the point of this is.

00:04:24.240 --> 00:04:25.410
No complaints!

00:04:26.030 --> 00:04:30.290
If you plan to enter a tournament with no actual experience,

00:04:30.290 --> 00:04:32.370
you'd better be able to handle this much.

00:04:32.870 --> 00:04:34.040
Tournament...

00:04:36.210 --> 00:04:37.710
And this...

00:04:41.300 --> 00:04:43.340
A storm in the great red spot!

00:05:16.290 --> 00:05:17.500
Okay, we're done.

00:05:17.500 --> 00:05:19.590
I have a good handle on your abilities now.

00:05:21.050 --> 00:05:23.980
The whole world's spinning...

00:05:23.980 --> 00:05:24.800
Can't go on...

00:05:28.890 --> 00:05:30.260
Hey, Kane!

00:05:30.260 --> 00:05:31.390
This is overdoing—

00:05:31.720 --> 00:05:32.740
Huh?

00:05:33.890 --> 00:05:35.140
I died.

00:05:35.140 --> 00:05:36.730
So did I.

00:05:43.480 --> 00:05:45.950
Like I thought... It was different.

00:05:46.700 --> 00:05:49.030
That was scary.

00:05:49.030 --> 00:05:51.700
That was really tough, wasn't it?

00:05:51.700 --> 00:05:54.410
I had a good time.

00:05:55.040 --> 00:06:01.790
But if no one's been in a dinghy, does that mean they've never been in a tournament, either?

00:06:04.960 --> 00:06:07.680
The official Nebula Cup database?

00:06:07.680 --> 00:06:11.350
Yes, I believe we can find records here.

00:06:12.670 --> 00:06:13.350
There it is.

00:06:13.810 --> 00:06:18.440
"Following the 13th Nebula Cup,
Hakuoh Academy Senior High School

00:06:18.440 --> 00:06:25.190
will be suspended for interfering with the race
and ignoring safety regulations for five years"?!

00:06:31.240 --> 00:06:33.700
Hakuoh sent a message that they'll be participating.

00:06:35.080 --> 00:06:37.120
So the time has finally come.

00:06:37.580 --> 00:06:39.830
I know how you must feel.

00:06:40.210 --> 00:06:43.750
I thought that they wouldn't participate.

00:06:43.750 --> 00:06:46.090
That was my expectation.

00:06:46.800 --> 00:06:50.930
Will we be able to handle them in our current state?

00:06:51.590 --> 00:06:55.600
Those demons at Hakuoh Academy...

00:06:55.600 --> 00:06:58.270
Chairwoman, I have an idea.

00:06:58.810 --> 00:06:59.560
An idea?

00:06:59.560 --> 00:07:02.520
If they won't follow the rules, we'll find someone else who won't either.

00:07:05.980 --> 00:07:06.900
Hello!

00:07:06.900 --> 00:07:09.450
This is the Harold Lloyd Insurance Union.

00:07:10.780 --> 00:07:12.660
I'm Show, your agent.

00:07:24.640 --> 00:07:25.710
Okay!

00:07:44.360 --> 00:07:46.520
Sorry I scared you.

00:07:46.520 --> 00:07:48.320
No, it's okay.

00:07:48.320 --> 00:07:51.530
But what brings you out here?

00:07:51.530 --> 00:07:53.820
I'm looking for Kane.

00:07:53.820 --> 00:07:56.410
His terminal's off.

00:07:56.410 --> 00:07:58.490
He was acting weird.

00:07:58.490 --> 00:08:00.660
Yeah... Yeah, he was!

00:08:00.660 --> 00:08:03.330
I think he's up to something.

00:08:06.170 --> 00:08:08.340
I had a good time.

00:08:08.340 --> 00:08:11.630
But as captain, it worries me.

00:08:11.630 --> 00:08:14.220
Well, I'll make him tell me tomorrow.

00:08:14.220 --> 00:08:17.560
Between the club and piracy, you're really busy.

00:08:17.560 --> 00:08:19.020
I really am.

00:08:19.020 --> 00:08:20.930
I want to compliment myself.

00:08:21.610 --> 00:08:26.650
But when one of the underclassmen is working hard, I have time to bring her a drink.

00:08:27.110 --> 00:08:28.610
Working hard?

00:08:28.610 --> 00:08:30.440
I am?

00:08:31.690 --> 00:08:34.780
I've never thought of it that way...

00:08:35.760 --> 00:08:38.280
I like yachts.

00:08:39.660 --> 00:08:45.420
When I'm working on them, I lose track of the time.

00:08:49.750 --> 00:08:51.840
The wind...

00:09:05.270 --> 00:09:06.850
I think I understand.

00:09:06.850 --> 00:09:07.650
Huh?

00:09:08.470 --> 00:09:11.050
No, it's nothing.

00:09:11.050 --> 00:09:12.650
Let me help.

00:09:12.650 --> 00:09:14.150
T-Thank...

00:09:24.910 --> 00:09:28.290
Someone is trying to go after the Katos.

00:09:30.290 --> 00:09:32.340
We were aware of this.

00:09:32.340 --> 00:09:33.760
The Bisque Company.

00:09:33.760 --> 00:09:36.930
Thugs that hang around the Port of Orion.

00:09:41.810 --> 00:09:43.430
They aren't from around here.

00:09:43.430 --> 00:09:49.400
That would explain why they're not aware of our treaty regarding Kato Marika.

00:09:50.110 --> 00:09:52.610
Regardless, we can't afford them any opportunity.

00:09:52.610 --> 00:09:56.860
It could lead to us fighting each other for the pirates' power.

00:09:57.240 --> 00:10:02.450
We'll have to teach them that, at times, ignorance is no excuse.

00:10:04.780 --> 00:10:06.660
Then, in terms of specifics...

00:10:10.580 --> 00:10:13.630
Why are you showing me this now?

00:10:19.200 --> 00:10:20.680
Him?

00:10:24.100 --> 00:10:26.480
I see... So that's it?

00:10:27.100 --> 00:10:34.230
That's why all these shady guys
have agreed to leave Marika alone.

00:10:34.230 --> 00:10:36.610
We're worried.

00:10:36.900 --> 00:10:39.490
For now, she's protected.

00:10:39.490 --> 00:10:42.530
But after she graduates from Hakuoh Academy...

00:10:44.160 --> 00:10:46.700
That's for her to decide.

00:10:46.700 --> 00:10:50.290
She can do as she likes.

00:10:57.880 --> 00:10:59.880
I like yachts.

00:11:00.930 --> 00:11:03.800
Why did I join the yacht club again?

00:11:22.700 --> 00:11:23.530
That's right.

00:11:24.830 --> 00:11:26.830
I wanted to go into space.

00:11:30.630 --> 00:11:33.000
What you like, huh?

00:11:39.330 --> 00:11:40.090
Yes?

00:11:40.090 --> 00:11:42.050
Captain, we have a job offer.

00:11:43.760 --> 00:11:45.260
A security job?

00:11:45.800 --> 00:11:48.310
That's an unusual thing to ask pirates to handle.

00:11:48.310 --> 00:11:50.230
Who's the client?

00:11:50.230 --> 00:11:52.480
The Nebula Cup Administration Committee.

00:11:53.650 --> 00:11:58.820
Someone is going to try to interfere with the race, so they want you to stop it.

00:11:59.240 --> 00:12:00.820
Trouble?

00:12:00.820 --> 00:12:04.030
I heard your yacht club is participating,

00:12:04.030 --> 00:12:06.330
so I thought it would be a good fit.

00:12:06.990 --> 00:12:09.040
That's true...

00:12:12.670 --> 00:12:15.670
All right. We'll take the job.

00:12:15.670 --> 00:12:17.800
That was a quick decision.

00:12:17.800 --> 00:12:19.130
Thanks!

00:12:19.130 --> 00:12:20.510
What are the details?

00:12:20.880 --> 00:12:23.470
I'll send you the details later, on paper.

00:12:23.470 --> 00:12:25.260
Give 'em a look.

00:12:25.260 --> 00:12:26.680
See ya.

00:12:29.660 --> 00:12:30.810
Sure about this?

00:12:30.810 --> 00:12:35.850
If you're working aboard the Bentenmaru,
you won't be able to participate in the race, right?

00:12:35.850 --> 00:12:38.070
No, I'll be in the race.

00:12:40.070 --> 00:12:45.030
I don't even know if we'll qualify yet, so things will work out.

00:13:02.380 --> 00:13:03.470
Okay!

00:13:03.470 --> 00:13:04.840
Everyone's here.

00:13:05.130 --> 00:13:06.300
What's that?

00:13:06.300 --> 00:13:07.550
No idea!

00:13:07.550 --> 00:13:08.680
Let's go.

00:13:09.350 --> 00:13:12.930
Um, Mr. Kane, why are we on the beach?

00:13:13.270 --> 00:13:15.640
I'm not your teacher... Call me "Coach"!

00:13:15.640 --> 00:13:16.600
Huh?

00:13:16.600 --> 00:13:17.480
Coach!

00:13:17.480 --> 00:13:18.940
Okay!

00:13:19.900 --> 00:13:22.110
Marika, um...

00:13:22.110 --> 00:13:24.450
Don't say it. My head hurts.

00:13:24.450 --> 00:13:27.570
Okay, Coach! Why are we on the beach?

00:13:27.570 --> 00:13:30.160
Glad you asked, Natalia!

00:13:31.740 --> 00:13:32.540
Today,

00:13:33.130 --> 00:13:36.870
we're holding the qualifier to decide
who will attend the Nebula Cup!

00:13:38.750 --> 00:13:40.250
U-Um, Coach...

00:13:40.250 --> 00:13:41.420
How?

00:13:41.420 --> 00:13:43.260
You want to know?

00:13:43.260 --> 00:13:47.300
The reason you were brought here in swimsuits?

00:13:47.300 --> 00:13:48.140
Y-Yes!

00:13:49.760 --> 00:13:50.470
It's...

00:13:51.060 --> 00:13:52.170
this!

00:14:00.930 --> 00:14:03.900
In a tournament, the important thing is not your skills,

00:14:03.900 --> 00:14:06.820
but the endurance and concentration to use them!

00:14:07.360 --> 00:14:12.660
The first three girls to make it to the buoy and back will represent us in the Nebula Cup!

00:14:13.490 --> 00:14:15.410
Um, really?

00:14:15.750 --> 00:14:18.080
This has nothing to do with dinghies!

00:14:18.080 --> 00:14:21.880
We've only used these a little in our marine sports class!

00:14:22.170 --> 00:14:23.750
That's plenty!

00:14:23.750 --> 00:14:26.420
The first-years haven't taken that class yet!

00:14:26.710 --> 00:14:28.970
Kane, are you seriously going to decide it—

00:14:28.970 --> 00:14:29.890
Coach!

00:14:30.300 --> 00:14:32.010
Do you think I'm kidding?

00:14:32.010 --> 00:14:37.520
If your body can't keep pace with your skills when it counts, you'll just endanger yourselves!

00:14:40.950 --> 00:14:43.110
Fine, I get it!

00:14:43.110 --> 00:14:44.480
I'll do it!

00:14:44.860 --> 00:14:45.980
Good!

00:14:46.530 --> 00:14:48.900
If I win this, I can go to the tournament.

00:14:48.900 --> 00:14:51.240
I'll do my best!

00:15:03.210 --> 00:15:04.420
Start!

00:15:14.200 --> 00:15:15.510
See you later!

00:15:15.510 --> 00:15:17.020
Excuse me.

00:15:19.690 --> 00:15:20.940
Gruier!

00:15:21.440 --> 00:15:25.230
Gruier... That's right. You can't swim...

00:15:25.230 --> 00:15:26.690
Just watch, Gruier.

00:15:27.230 --> 00:15:27.940
I'll avenge you, no matter what!

00:15:27.940 --> 00:15:29.400
Are you okay?

00:15:29.400 --> 00:15:30.360
I'll avenge you, no matter what!

00:15:34.990 --> 00:15:38.870
Since I said I'd do it, I'll try my best to win!

00:15:39.660 --> 00:15:44.040
I have to enjoy everything I can now.

00:15:49.300 --> 00:15:50.970
Okay, this is a good wind.

00:15:58.850 --> 00:16:00.930
Everyone, do your best!

00:16:00.930 --> 00:16:02.560
Who do you think will win?

00:16:02.560 --> 00:16:04.860
I bought ice cream at the beach house!

00:16:05.730 --> 00:16:06.860
So, a question.

00:16:06.860 --> 00:16:09.440
Why are you here?!

00:16:09.440 --> 00:16:12.450
We're in charge of the brain work.

00:16:12.450 --> 00:16:14.110
Not here you're not!

00:16:14.410 --> 00:16:16.330
Fifty laps, up and down the beach!

00:16:47.020 --> 00:16:48.770
It's almost time.

00:16:58.160 --> 00:17:00.660
Hey, are you sure about this?

00:17:00.660 --> 00:17:01.660
Why not?

00:17:01.660 --> 00:17:03.210
Kane said to do it.

00:17:03.210 --> 00:17:05.330
If we're doing it, do it!

00:17:05.330 --> 00:17:08.130
I'm not used to this!

00:17:08.130 --> 00:17:10.090
You're pretty talented, Misa.

00:17:10.090 --> 00:17:10.960
Hurry!

00:17:15.380 --> 00:17:16.640
Target locked.

00:17:17.030 --> 00:17:17.590
Fire.

00:17:35.820 --> 00:17:38.490
Don't tell me the Bentenmaru did this.

00:17:40.370 --> 00:17:42.170
Hey, are you sure about this?

00:17:42.170 --> 00:17:43.160
Why not?

00:17:43.500 --> 00:17:44.870
Amazing.

00:17:44.870 --> 00:17:45.870
S-Shut up!

00:17:46.160 --> 00:17:48.330
What are you thinking, Kane?

00:17:48.330 --> 00:17:50.340
After that, no one will be left standing.

00:17:53.560 --> 00:17:54.300
Okay!

00:17:54.300 --> 00:17:56.010
I'm gonna catch up!

00:17:59.220 --> 00:18:00.680
Everyone is amazing!

00:18:01.810 --> 00:18:03.140
You've gotta be kidding me.

00:18:04.270 --> 00:18:11.360
Whenever my club's in trouble, they get really good...

00:18:17.570 --> 00:18:19.240
First is Natalia!

00:18:22.450 --> 00:18:24.370
Second is Grunhilde!

00:18:25.290 --> 00:18:27.330
Pardon me.

00:18:27.620 --> 00:18:29.040
Is that okay?

00:18:29.040 --> 00:18:31.750
Splendid, Grunhilde.

00:18:31.750 --> 00:18:33.300
I-I guess so...

00:18:33.750 --> 00:18:36.340
You guys always get to do the fun stuff.

00:18:36.340 --> 00:18:38.510
Once in a while, we'll take the lead.

00:18:47.180 --> 00:18:48.980
No way!

00:18:49.440 --> 00:18:52.940
These girls are all totally nuts.

00:18:53.480 --> 00:18:56.650
Marika, I won't lose!

00:18:56.650 --> 00:18:58.320
I'll try for real too.

00:18:58.320 --> 00:18:58.900
Right!

00:19:19.550 --> 00:19:20.800
Goal!

00:19:20.800 --> 00:19:23.100
Third place goes to Ai Hoshimiya!

00:19:28.600 --> 00:19:30.270
I did it! I did it!

00:19:32.520 --> 00:19:35.440
It was just supposed to be a little joke.

00:19:35.440 --> 00:19:37.400
I was pretty surprised.

00:19:37.400 --> 00:19:39.950
That was a nasty joke!

00:19:39.950 --> 00:19:43.370
I don't know why you did it, but don't do it again.

00:19:44.280 --> 00:19:45.450
You're right.

00:19:45.950 --> 00:19:49.870
By the way, what would you have done if you'd won?

00:19:49.870 --> 00:19:51.420
We have a job, right?

00:19:51.830 --> 00:19:55.090
I had a few ideas.

00:19:55.090 --> 00:19:59.670
I thought it might be fun to pirate while racing.

00:20:00.010 --> 00:20:01.680
Greedy.

00:20:01.680 --> 00:20:02.760
Am I?

00:20:02.760 --> 00:20:06.430
Yeah, but that's perfect for a pirate.

00:20:06.430 --> 00:20:07.390
Yeah.

00:20:07.390 --> 00:20:09.060
But I feel good.

00:20:09.390 --> 00:20:14.520
This means Ai likes yachts more than I do now.

00:20:15.440 --> 00:20:19.000
Then what do ya like now?

00:20:19.000 --> 00:20:22.320
What's with this "ya" business, Kane?!

00:20:22.320 --> 00:20:25.570
Oh, yeah... Sorry, Captain.

00:20:29.880 --> 00:20:33.080
Okay, we have our entrants.

00:20:33.080 --> 00:20:38.590
I'll keep training everyone, those who are and those who aren't entering, until the tournament!

00:20:38.590 --> 00:20:39.880
Right...

00:20:40.510 --> 00:20:43.340
But first, we have to replenish those calories you used up.

00:20:43.840 --> 00:20:47.550
Your next order is to go to the Lamp House and eat parfaits!

00:20:48.290 --> 00:20:49.600
My treat.

00:20:49.600 --> 00:20:53.270
Yay! Yeah!

00:21:02.140 --> 00:21:03.570
President...

00:21:03.570 --> 00:21:05.990
What are you doing here?

00:21:05.990 --> 00:21:08.740
Can't go on...

00:21:11.500 --> 00:21:21.210
<i>We're Hakuoh, the great white birds...</i>

00:21:21.210 --> 00:21:25.840
<i>Hoist the sails and watch the wind...</i>

00:21:26.130 --> 00:21:27.840
Compressor on line.

00:21:27.840 --> 00:21:30.510
Output at 97%.

00:21:30.510 --> 00:21:32.310
Output error within tolerance.

00:21:32.930 --> 00:21:34.310
Electronics functioning properly.

00:21:34.770 --> 00:21:38.310
Sub-space is clear, and the waves are high.

00:21:38.900 --> 00:21:41.530
The girls' ship has left port too.

00:21:43.770 --> 00:21:44.780
This is control.

00:21:45.180 --> 00:21:47.360
Bentenmaru, you are cleared for launch.

00:21:47.360 --> 00:21:49.160
You are cleared for launch.

